From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:27:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: psci: Mark the idle states unusable without
 CPU_SUSPEND

psci_init_cpu_suspend() asks the firmware for PSCI_FEATURES(CPU_SUSPEND),
but on NOT_SUPPORTED it only leaves the feature flags at zero, and
cpuidle-psci registers every DT idle state as usable. Each entry is then
an SMC that returns an error: cpuidle counts it as rejected and the
governor picks the same state again, so an idle CPU loops through
cpu_pm_enter() and the firmware call instead of staying in WFI. Forced
idle from the idle injection cooling device takes the same path.

Record the refusal in the PSCI driver and declare it in linux/psci.h as
psci_cpu_suspend_supported(), and let cpuidle-psci mark every PSCI state
CPUIDLE_FLAG_UNUSABLE when it is false. The driver still registers, so
WFI and the idle cooling devices stay. SYSTEM_SUSPEND is already gated
on the same query.

Firmware before PSCI 1.0 has no PSCI_FEATURES and is assumed to support
CPU_SUSPEND, as before. Firmware that reports CPU_SUSPEND sees no change.

Not covered: firmware that implements CPU_SUSPEND but refuses a given
power_state parameter, which PSCI_FEATURES does not report.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards whose firmware implements
CPU_SUSPEND; the idle states stayed usable and were entered. Not
triggered: firmware without CPU_SUSPEND.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c   | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 include/linux/psci.h           |  1 +
 3 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
index b250d0dde760..4ceb9627c46f 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
@@ -409,6 +409,22 @@ static int psci_idle_init_cpu(struct device *dev, int cpu)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The DT describes the states, the firmware decides whether they can be
+	 * entered. Without CPU_SUSPEND every entry is an SMC that returns an
+	 * error, and the governor picks the same state again. Keep the driver,
+	 * WFI and the cooling device registered below still need it, and make
+	 * the PSCI states unusable.
+	 */
+	if (!psci_cpu_suspend_supported()) {
+		int i;
+
+		for (i = 1; i < drv->state_count; i++)
+			drv->states[i].flags |= CPUIDLE_FLAG_UNUSABLE;
+		pr_warn_once("firmware refuses CPU_SUSPEND, %d DT idle state(s) unusable\n",
+			     drv->state_count - 1);
+	}
+
 	ret = cpuidle_register(drv, NULL);
 	if (ret)
 		goto deinit;
diff --git a/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c b/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
index e73bae6cb23a..9d697988fbca 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/psci/psci.c
@@ -77,6 +77,7 @@ struct psci_0_1_function_ids get_psci_0_1_function_ids(void)
 				PSCI_1_0_EXT_POWER_STATE_TYPE_MASK)
 
 static u32 psci_cpu_suspend_feature;
+static bool psci_cpu_suspend_refused;
 static bool psci_system_reset2_supported;
 static bool psci_system_off2_hibernate_supported;
 
@@ -91,6 +92,16 @@ bool psci_has_osi_support(void)
 	return psci_cpu_suspend_feature & PSCI_1_0_OS_INITIATED;
 }
 
+/*
+ * False only when the firmware has said so: PSCI_FEATURES(CPU_SUSPEND)
+ * answered NOT_SUPPORTED. Before PSCI 1.0 there is no PSCI_FEATURES to ask,
+ * and CPU_SUSPEND is assumed, as it always has been.
+ */
+bool psci_cpu_suspend_supported(void)
+{
+	return !psci_cpu_suspend_refused;
+}
+
 static inline bool psci_power_state_loses_context(u32 state)
 {
 	const u32 mask = psci_has_ext_power_state() ?
@@ -596,8 +607,12 @@ static void __init psci_init_cpu_suspend(void)
 {
 	int feature = psci_features(PSCI_FN_NATIVE(0_2, CPU_SUSPEND));
 
-	if (feature != PSCI_RET_NOT_SUPPORTED)
+	if (feature != PSCI_RET_NOT_SUPPORTED) {
 		psci_cpu_suspend_feature = feature;
+	} else {
+		psci_cpu_suspend_refused = true;
+		pr_info("CPU_SUSPEND not supported by firmware\n");
+	}
 }
 
 /*
diff --git a/include/linux/psci.h b/include/linux/psci.h
index 4ca0060a3fc4..ccc42c65d014 100644
--- a/include/linux/psci.h
+++ b/include/linux/psci.h
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ int psci_cpu_suspend_enter(u32 state);
 bool psci_power_state_is_valid(u32 state);
 int psci_set_osi_mode(bool enable);
 bool psci_has_osi_support(void);
+bool psci_cpu_suspend_supported(void);
 
 struct psci_operations {
 	u32 (*get_version)(void);
